<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="gear-before-raiding">Gear you can aim for before raiding</h3>There are certain gear pieces that generally do not fit into this guide as they aren't truly considered pre-bis as they require <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>. However it is possible to get them from weekly heroic dungeons as well, so this section will be dedicated to them.<br/>
<br/>You can gain 1600 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> every week from doing 7 heroics or 4 zandalari heroics, and you can do them in a single day. As a balance druid, you will want to get <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71107/obsidian-arborweave-gloves">
<img alt="Obsidian Arborweave Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_leather_raiddruid_j_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Arborweave Gloves</span></a> first followed by <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71110/obsidian-arborweave-vestment">
<img alt="Obsidian Arborweave Vestment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_raiddruid_j_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Arborweave Vestment</span></a> and then <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71109/obsidian-arborweave-leggings">
<img alt="Obsidian Arborweave Leggings" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_leather_raiddruid_j_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Arborweave Leggings</span></a>. The order for this is based on the 2 first items have our best stats while legs have crit and our t11 legs which is what you'd wear as your second best pre-bis have our best stats so it contains the lowest gain from ugprading. After the 3 tier pieces, which we will use for all of tier 12, there are a few choices to make. You can grab <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71214/firemind-pendant">
<img alt="Firemind Pendant" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_neck_hyjaldaily_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Firemind Pendant</span></a> for a neck upgrade or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71262/smolderskull-bindings">
<img alt="Smolderskull Bindings" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_leather_raiddruid_j_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Smolderskull Bindings</span></a> if you need wrist upgrades, although the wrists are boe and can also be bought with an alt or from other players. Last there's relic where we want <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71148/soulflame-vial">
<img alt="Soulflame Vial" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cat_trinket02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soulflame Vial</span></a>. There is also <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71149/singed-plume-of-aviana">
<img alt="Singed Plume of Aviana" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_feather_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Singed Plume of Aviana</span></a> but it just has less total offstats with no compensation anywhere, so it makes no sense to go for it since both relics have our most desirable stats. <b>Always buy the 3 tier pieces first and only then go for one of the other items on the list. Relic lasts longest but is typically a smaller upgrade than neck or wrist.</b>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="elemental-rune-dungeons">Explanation of Elemental Rune Dungeons</h3>With the release of Rage of the Firelands, we get a new dungeon system called Elemental Rune Dungeons. In this system you get <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a> from killing bosses, 2 for each boss you kill and if you don't skip any bosses, the final boss awards an additional 3. Over half the items in this list is obtained from this system, and to queue for it you will require 346 ilvl. It is therefore recommended that as soon as you can queue for these dungeons, you make that a priority. You can get almost full pre-BiS from these dungeons, only missing a few items.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="body-armor">Body Armor for Balance Druid DPS</h3>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="head-for-balance-druid-dps">Head for Balance Druid DPS</h4>With the new inferno protocol letting us grab <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60282/stormriders-cover">
<img alt="Stormrider's Cover" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_leather_raiddruid_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stormrider's Cover</span></a> head and shoulders from dungeons, that will be our best alternative until we can step foot inside raids. We can still use <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=59453/camouflage-bio-optic-killshades">
<img alt="Camouflage Bio-Optic Killshades" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gizmo_newgoggles.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Camouflage Bio-Optic Killshades</span></a> if <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60282/stormriders-cover">
<img alt="Stormrider's Cover" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_leather_raiddruid_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stormrider's Cover</span></a> can't be combined with another tier piece for 2set or 4set bonus, for example if you have tier 11 in every slot, but as soon as you start upgrading to tier 12 in some slots you will want <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60282/stormriders-cover">
<img alt="Stormrider's Cover" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_leather_raiddruid_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stormrider's Cover</span></a>. However even in this case, it is preferable to run <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60282/stormriders-cover">
<img alt="Stormrider's Cover" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_leather_raiddruid_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stormrider's Cover</span></a> and rather get 372 legs from the bags you can buy with throne of four winds loot, this is covered more in the section about legs.<br/>
<br/>
<a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/news/what-to-buy-with-fissure-stone-fragments-from-elemental-rune-dungeons-cataclysm-348669">Wowhead has an article about these dungeons which will show you all available items and their original sources</a>
<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Helm Enchant</b>: <a class="q7 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62367/arcanum-of-hyjal">
<img alt="Arcanum of Hyjal" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_masterofelements.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Arcanum of Hyjal</span></a>, requires Revered reputation with <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1158/guardians-of-hyjal">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Guardians of Hyjal</span></a>.<div class="pad"></div>
