<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="legs-for-balance-druid-dps">Legs for Balance Druid DPS</h4>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=65384/gale-rouser-leggings">
<img alt="Gale Rouser Leggings" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_leather_raiddruid_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gale Rouser Leggings</span></a> is our best pre-raid item and what we will want to use as our off-piece. For those unfamiliar with the term off-piece, it refers to an item that goes into the same slot as a tier item (head/<wbr/>shoulder/<wbr/>chest/<wbr/>hands/<wbr/>legs) but we use a non-tier item since only 4 of the 5 slots need tier items for us to get all our set bonuses. The suffix on the legs does not matter, it will be our best pre-raid option as long as using a different leg does not allow us to achieve a set bonus. Here we follow the same rules for suffixes when it comes to belt and prioritize in the order of  <b>Undertow (Haste and Spirit) &gt; Feverflare (Haste and Mastery) &gt; Wavecrest (Mastery and Spirit) &gt; Fireflash (Haste and Crit)</b>.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60283/stormriders-leggings">
<img alt="Stormrider's Leggings" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_leather_raiddruid_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stormrider's Leggings</span></a> is a strong alternative for pre-raid bis, and can be bought in order to get tier bonus until you can get helm and shoulders, which will depend on how fast you prioritize getting tier from <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a>. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69613/leggings-of-the-pride">
<img alt="Leggings of the Pride" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_leather_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leggings of the Pride</span></a> is an okay alternative, but being from an amani dungeon it suffers from the drawback that going for it does not help you towards gaining more <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a>. Outside of this just grab the highest ilvl legs you come across, but do avoid spending justice points on any legs that aren't <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60283/stormriders-leggings">
<img alt="Stormrider's Leggings" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_leather_raiddruid_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stormrider's Leggings</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>Keep in mind that when we are 4 weeks into Rage of the Firelands patch (19th november for US, 20th november for EU) our BiS leg piece is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71109/obsidian-arborweave-leggings">
<img alt="Obsidian Arborweave Leggings" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_leather_raiddruid_j_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Arborweave Leggings</span></a>. Additionally during week 2 of Rage of the Firelands patch (5th-12th november for US, 6th-13th november for EU) we will have T12 gloves which results in us needing to use <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60283/stormriders-leggings">
<img alt="Stormrider's Leggings" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_leather_raiddruid_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stormrider's Leggings</span></a> to maintain our 4set and is therefore our BiS for that week.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Leg Armor:</b> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=54450/powerful-ghostly-spellthread">
<img alt="Powerful Ghostly Spellthread" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_astralrecalgroup.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Powerful Ghostly Spellthread</span></a>
