<a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=1637/orgrimmar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Orgrimmar</span></a> (H) or <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=1519/stormwind-city">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Stormwind City</span></a> (A)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<div class="pad"></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="trinkets-for-balance-druid-dps">Trinkets for Balance Druid DPS</h4>Trinkets are often less reliant on ilvl. They also have certain interesting and unique uses, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56400/sorrowsong">
<img alt="Sorrowsong" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_invisibilitytotem.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sorrowsong</span></a> is an extremely strong trinket for fights when the boss stays under 35% for extended times or when your raid group is missing the DPS to beat a soft enrage in last phase. In such cases it goes from a bad trinket to your best trinket. This is why trinkets must be looked at more on a case by case basis instead of mostly just looking at ilvl like rest of our gear.<br/>
<br/>In terms of trinket rankings, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62047/darkmoon-card-volcano">
<img alt="Darkmoon Card: Volcano" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_tarot_volcanocard.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmoon Card: Volcano</span></a> is incredibly strong and our best trinket not only pre-raid, but the entirety of phase 3. The trinket we use in our second trinket slot is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=65105/theralions-mirror">
<img alt="Theralion's Mirror" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_arcane_teleportironforge.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Theralion's Mirror</span></a>. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=65053/bell-of-enraging-resonance">
<img alt="Bell of Enraging Resonance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bell_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bell of Enraging Resonance</span></a> is not far behind and if you can't afford Volcano then you can use this one until you can save up the gold. The reamining trinkets are far behind.<br/>
<br/>For the remainder of the trinkets, there is:<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70142/moonwell-chalice">
<img alt="Moonwell Chalice" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_potion_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Moonwell Chalice</span></a> Very strong trinket that will see niche uses in fights where we Solar Camp (see rotation for more info). Worth getting but a 3 week grind to obtain.<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58183/soul-casket">
<img alt="Soul Casket" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Casket</span></a> strong alternative and reliable to get with flexibility from reforging, has an on-use you have to remember to use. If you run out of things to spend justice points on before you have trinkets you can use this one temporairly.<br/>
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56320/witching-hourglass">
<img alt="Witching Hourglass" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gizmo_khoriumpowercore.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Witching Hourglass</span></a> Is one of our stronger pre-raid trinkets and can be obtained as a lucky drop while just grinding <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a>. It is no longer worth specifically farming as there are several better trinkets that are reliable to get, even if not dropping gold on <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62047/darkmoon-card-volcano">
<img alt="Darkmoon Card: Volcano" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_tarot_volcanocard.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmoon Card: Volcano</span></a>.<br/>
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56462/gale-of-shadows">
<img alt="Gale of Shadows" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_gathershadows.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gale of Shadows</span></a> is a strong overall trinket with the ability to flex some haste into hit<div class="pad"></div>
